Intent: stop the repeated expected Windows verifier error emitted by local HTTPS discovery without accepting an untrusted certificate.
Result: app_log owns an exact-target Tokio task-local filter; only the local HTTPS send enters that scope; HTTP, CEF, the TLS backend, and every unrelated request remain unchanged.
Tests: TDD reproduced one escaped verifier record before the fix and zero after it while the self-signed certificate remained rejected. Contract tests preserve the same verifier log outside the scope and unrelated logs inside it.
